WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.073
We have a great show tonight.

00:00:02.073 --> 00:00:03.320
(ringing)
Hold on just a second.

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:06.810
I am told I'm getting a
Zoom call from, really?

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.430
One of my writers, yes.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.260
Oh, it's Laurie Kilmartin. Hey Laurie.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.330
Hi Conan, how's it going?

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.330
It's going great.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:14.560
Is it okay if I call you back?

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.840
'Cause I'm taping a show right now.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:17.910
Oh, I won't keep you.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.450
I just wondered when you have a minute,

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.873
could you write me a
letter of recommendation?

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.200
Letter of recommendation,
like a job recommendation?

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.820
Yeah, I'm trying to apply for this job.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:28.943
Here, let me show you.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.830
Prince William and Kate Middleton

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:35.090
are on the hunt for a
housekeeper with discretion.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:37.740
Wait, you want to be a
housekeeper for the royal family?

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.500
Oh, very much.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.860
Okay, I get that you're
a big fan of the royals.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.490
I've always known that, but Laurie,

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:46.550
you're an incredible standup
comic with a great career.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:47.590
And you're a writer for me.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:50.400
I mean, that's like the Holy Grail.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.050
Why would you want to be a housekeeper?

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.280
Well, I don't know,

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.780
I guess because Kensington
Palace would be my house.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.250
I see.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:00:59.310
Do you see?

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:02.020
Look, this is my current house.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.927
[Conan] Okay. It's nice enough, yeah.

00:01:03.927 --> 00:01:06.730
[Laurie] And this would
be my future house.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:08.970
[Conan] Okay, I get it, I get it, yeah.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:10.790
So let's just shuttle back and forth

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:12.160
between the two, shall we?

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.950
Tell me if you could spot any differences.

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.713
Okay. No, no, no, no.
My house, their house.

00:01:15.713 --> 00:01:17.060
[Conan] You don't have
to do that, I get it.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:18.644
My house, their house.
I get it, I get it.

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:20.045
My house, their house.
I get it, stop.

00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:20.878
My house, their house.
Stop, that's fine.

00:01:20.878 --> 00:01:22.080
But Laurie, the job post says

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.170
they're looking for a
housekeeper with discretion.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.100
That means whatever you saw,

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.773
you'd have to keep it to yourself.

00:01:27.773 --> 00:01:28.810
Do you think you can do that?

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:31.240
Conan, I worked for you for 10 years

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.540
and I've never told anyone

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:35.240
that you have a panic
attack before every show.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.230
Well, I don't think it's every show.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.700
Every single night, full-blown panic.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:42.260
You grab your producer
Jeff, and you start crying

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.760
and you say, "they're
gonna eat me alive, mommy."

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.260
And then he has to slap you

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.930
and you start crying
harder, "hold me, mommy."

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:49.990
All right, all right, all right.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:52.140
You know what? I'll write you
a recommendation, all right?

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.140
And what about that
time you tried to start

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.210
hoop skirt Mondays at the office.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:59.073
Only you showed up in a
giant blue hoop skirt,

00:01:59.073 --> 00:01:59.906
no one else did.

00:01:59.906 --> 00:02:00.739
Wait a minute, wait a minute.

00:02:00.739 --> 00:02:01.580
I said I'd write your recommendation,

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.160
and it wasn't a bad idea.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.270
I could have, but I never mentioned

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.230
your Anthony Michael Hall back tattoo.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:08.080
I could have.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.510
He was great in "Johnny Be Good."

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:12.450
You paid someone to chew your food for you

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.890
and you say "baby bird want his lunchie."

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:16.570
All right, all right,
we're good, we're good.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:19.010
I'll write you the recommendation, okay?

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:21.760
Thank you. Thanks.
(disconnection ding)

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.250
Got a terrific show.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.430
Ricky Gervais gonna be joining us.

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:28.130
We'll take a break, we'll be right back.

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:30.420
I'm getting hungry.
(relaxed music)

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:31.770
Andy, can you chew my food?

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.683
Baby bird wants his lunchie!

00:02:36.748 --> 00:02:38.398
All right, I'll be right there.

